# Why this Module ships no seed/ directory.
# A marker with no justification is a silent skip in file form; lint-config
# refuses an empty one.

Redis is a cache and a Celery broker. Its content is created and consumed at
runtime and deliberately survives only through AOF in the redis-data volume; a
pre-seeded key would be a stale cache entry or a phantom queued task.
conf/redis.conf is configuration, bind-mounted read-only, not seed.
